# Agent scratch (subagent-driven-development ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Local run artifacts
# Tower/soak runs are routinely captured to a log file (see the soak-test
# section in README.md). Those logs carry per-frame observation metadata
# and must not be committed -- Rule 12, resource/privacy discipline.
*.log

# Environment / secrets
.env

# Object memory's default store path (relative data/object_memory) --
# real observation history must never be swept up by a broad `git add`.
data/

# Operator brief for an autonomous run; an input to the work, not part of it.
plan.md
planned-cartridges.md

# Measurement output. The SCRIPTS under scripts/research/ are committed --
# a benchmark nobody can rerun is an anecdote -- but their output is not:
# a per-detection dump over the real corpus is 21 MB, it is derived from
# imagery this repository does not carry, and it is regenerated by one
# command. Findings belong in docs/superpowers/research/, where they can
# be read.
analysis/
